        "body": "Resolves #1670\n\n`withCacheIsolation` was typed to return `T`, but the wrapper is async, so a synchronous handler's result came back as a Promise while the type said otherwise.\n\nThe returned handler is now typed as `(event: H3Event) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<T>>>`, and keeps the properties of the wrapped handler (such as ocache's `invalidate`) through `Pick<T, keyof T>`. No runtime change.\n\nAdded type tests for a sync and an async handler and for a copied property. `pnpm typecheck`, the type tests, the cache and route rules tests, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm build` pass.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Updated the `withCacheIsolation` type to reflect that wrapped handlers return a promise, making the result type clearer for callers.\n  * Preserved the wrapped handler’s properties and their original types in the returned type.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
